<section class="faq-section" style="padding: 50px 0; background: #0b132b; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 25px; text-align: center;">
      Frequently Asked Questions &bull; Movers To Move Packers And Movers
    </h2>
    
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">What documents are required for a GST‑compliant move with packers and movers to move within 2 house?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">For GST‑compliant relocation you need a valid GSTIN certificate, a signed quotation, the e‑Way bill generated based on the invoice value, identity proof of the consignor, and a copy of the rental or ownership deed of the origin and destination premises. These documents satisfy both tax regulations and IBA standards, ensuring a smooth intercity transfer.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">How is the insurance premium calculated for a 2‑house shift across 1499 km?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">The premium is a percentage of the declared value of the goods, typically 0.5‑1% of the total insured amount. Factors influencing the rate include the nature of items (fragile, high‑value), total weight, and the chosen coverage tier. Our IRDAI‑approved policy guarantees full reimbursement up to the declared value if any loss occurs during transit.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Can I track my household goods in real time during the NH 19 transit?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Yes. All our container trucks are equipped with satellite GPS units that feed live location data to our customer portal. You can view the exact position, estimated arrival time, and any checkpoint stops. Real‑time tracking adds transparency and peace of mind for customers moving within 2 house.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">What makes your 7‑layer packaging system superior for moving delicate items?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">The system combines high‑density bubble cushioning, multi‑ply corrugated sheets, reinforced wooden crates, and weather‑proof stretch film. Each layer addresses a specific risk—impact, vibration, moisture, and crushing. This holistic approach reduces damage probability by over 90%, making it ideal for glassware, temple idols, and electronics during long‑haul moves.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">How does the cost matrix differ for a 2‑house move versus a single‑house relocation?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">A 2‑house shift involves transporting belongings from two separate origins to a single destination, effectively doubling loading, unloading, and handling efforts. The cost matrix reflects additional labor, extra fuel for the extra distance, and higher insurance coverage. However, consolidating both moves in one trip can still be more economical than booking two independent services.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">Are there any special regulations at checkposts along NH 19 that I should be aware of?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Yes. Checkposts require a valid e‑Way bill, vehicle registration, and driver ID. Certain states may inspect packaging integrity and verify insurance documents. Our transit advisory team prepares all paperwork in advance and informs drivers of scheduled stops, ensuring compliance and minimizing delays.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px 20px;">
        <h3 style="color: #f8fafc; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 8px;">What is the typical transit time for a 1499 km move from Movers to Move?</h3>
        <p style="color: #cbd5e1; line-height: 1.7; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;">Under normal traffic conditions, the journey along NH 19 takes approximately 28‑32 hours of driving time, spread over 2‑3 days to allow for mandatory driver rest periods, checkpoint clearances, and safe loading/unloading. Our route performance highlights guarantee adherence to this schedule, barring unforeseen weather or road incidents.</p>
      </div>
  </div>
